      "text": "Since $x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4$, we square both sides to find:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 &= 4^2, \\\\\nx^2 - 2\\left(x \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\right) + \\frac{1}{x^2} &= 16, \\\\\nx^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} - 2 &= 16, \\\\\nx^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} &= 18.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, let's find the cubic expression $x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3}$:\n\\begin{align*}\nx^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} &= \\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} + 1\\right), \\\\\n&= 4(18 + 1), \\\\\n&= 76.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{76}$.",
